ince 1923, has a current dividend yield of 1.5292959213% and has increased its dividends for 15 successive years.\n\nMarsh & McLennan Companies Inc.'s market cap is $ 105,034,827,760 and has a PE ratio of 26.12. The stock price closed yesterday at $ 213.17 and has a 52 week low/high of $ 207.21 and $ 248.00.\n\nMarsh & McLennan Companies, Inc. is a professional services firm offering services in areas of risk, strategy and people. Co.'s Risk and Insurance Services segment includes risk management activities (risk advice, risk transfer and risk control and mitigation solutions) as well as insurance and reinsurance broking and services. This segment operates through Marsh and Guy Carpenter. Marsh provides data-driven risk advisory services and insurance solutions to commercial and consumer clients. Guy Carpenter develops advanced risk, reinsurance and capital strategies.\n\n#### For more information on Marsh & McLennan Companies Inc. click here.\n\nMarsh & McLennan Companies Inc. current dividend information as per the date of this press release is:\n\nDividend Declaration Date: July 09, 2025\nDividend Ex Date: July 24, 2025\nDividend Record Date: July 24, 2025\nDividend Payment Date: August 15, 2025\nDividend Amount: $ 0.9000\n\n\n#### MMC LINKS\n\nMMC Dividend History Detail\nMMC Projected 10 Year Dividend Yield\nMMC Dividend News\nMMC Competitors News--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMarsh McLennan increases quarterly dividend by 10 percent By Investing.com (https://ca.investing.com/news/company-news/marsh-mclennan-increases-quarterly-dividend-by-10-percent-93CH-4095447)\nciteturn11search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; \n\n# Marsh McLennan increases quarterly dividend by 10 percent\n\nPublished 2025-07-09, 11:28 a/m\n\nImage: Marsh McLennan increases quarterly dividend by 10 percent\n\nMarsh McLennan increases quarterly dividend by 10 percent\n\nIn this article:\n\nMRSH-0.39%\n\nNEW YORK - Marsh McLennan (NYSE:MMC) announced Wednesday that its Board of Directors has approved a 10% increase in the company's quarterly dividend, raising it from $0.815 to $0.900 per share on outstanding common stock. This marks the company's 15th consecutive year of dividend increases, with a current yield of 1.53%. According to InvestingPro analysis, MMC has maintained dividend payments for 55 consecutive years.\n\nThe higher dividend will be payable on August 15, 2025, to stockholders of record as of July 24, 2025, according to a company press release.\n\nMarsh McLennan operates globally in risk, strategy and people advisory services through four business segments: Marsh, Guy Carpenter, Mercer and Oliver Wyman. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevvity Maintains $0.07 Quarterly Dividend, Payable August 2025 | PKI Stock News (https://www.stocktitan.net/news/PKI/revvity-board-declares-quarterly-thykxmtpa5ve.html)\nciteturn11search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; \n\n# Revvity Board Declares Quarterly Dividend\n\nRhea-AI Impact\n\n(Neutral)\n\nRhea-AI Sentiment\n\n(Neutral)\n\nTags\n\ndividends\n\n04/24/2025 - 04:05 PM\n\nWALTHAM, Mass.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- The Board of Directors of Revvity (NYSE: RVTY), today declared a regular quarterly dividend of $0.07 per share of common stock. This dividend is payable on August 8, 2025 to all shareholders of record at the close of business on July 18, 2025.\n\nAbout Revvity\nAt Revvity, “impossible” is inspiration, and “can’t be done” is a call to action. Revvity provides health science solutions, technologies, expertise and services that deliver complete workflows from discovery to development, and diagnosis to cure. Revvity is revolutionizing what’s possible in healthcare, with specialized focus areas in translational multi-omics technologies, biomarker identification, imaging, prediction, screening, detection and diagnosis, informatics and more.\n\nWith 2024 revenue of more than $2.7 billion and approximately 11,000 employees, Revvity serves customers across pharmaceutical and biotech, diagnostic labs, academia and governments. It is part of the S&P 500 index and has customers in more than 160 countries.\n\nStay updated by following our Newsroom, LinkedIn, X, YouTube, Facebook and Instagram.\n\nImage\n\nView source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250424490742/en/\n\nMedia Relations:\nChet Murray\n(781) 462-5126\nchet.murray@revvity.com\n\nInvestor Relations:\nSteve Willoughby\nsteve.willoughby@revvity.com\n\nSource: Revvity--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOMMITTEE OF THE WHOLE AGENDA (https://www.stlouiscountymn.gov/Portals/0/Library/Dept/Auditor/County-Board/2026-06-09%20Committee%20of%20the%20Whole%20Agenda.pdf?ver=OrtJQLG74i7Cz35BudFc-g%3D%3D)\nciteturn11search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; \nPolicy Objectives: \nMinnesota Statutes § 375.32 and County Purchasing Rules have been followed in obtaining a \nproposal and for authority in carrying such coverage.  \n \nFiscal/Budget Impacts/Funding Source/FTE Considerations: \nMarsh McLennan Agency, LLC will provide property and related insurance coverage on major \nstructures, equipment, amended contents and boiler and machinery from the Chubb Group of \nInsurance Companies at a premium of $621,046.45 for the period July 24, 2025, through July 24, \n2027.  Funding for property insurance is payable from fund 720, Agency 720001, Object \n635100. \n \nRecommendation: \nIt is recommended that the St. Louis County Board authorizes the purchase of property and \nrelated insurance coverage on major structures, equipment, amended contents and boiler and \nmachinery from the Chubb Group of Insurance Companies through Marsh McLennan Agency, \nLLC at a premium of $621,046.45 for the period July 24, 2026, through July 24, 2027. Funding \nfor property insurance is payable from Fund 720, Agency 720001, Object 635100. \n \nIt is further recommended the County Board authorizes the addition and/or deletion of property \nfrom the policy as required throughout the policy period.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevvity - 10-K annual report 2025 (https://companiesmarketcap.com/revvity/sec-reports-10k/0000031791-26-000012/)\nciteturn11search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \nWe expect to repay the 2026 Notes with our existing cash on hand or borrowings under our senior unsecured revolving credit facility, or a combination thereof.\n\nIn addition, o n January 7, 2025, our prior senior unsecured revolving credit facility was cancelled and replaced with a new senior unsecured revolving credit facility with a five-year term and a borrowing capacity of $1.5 billion available through January 7, 2030.\n\nDividends\n\nOur Board of Directors (our “Board”) declared a regular quarterly cash dividend of $0.07 per share in each quarter of fiscal years 2025, 2024 and 2023, resulting in an annual dividend rate of $0.28 per share. At December 28, 2025, we had accrued $7.8 million for a dividend declared in October 2025 for the fourth quarter of fiscal year 2025 that was paid in February 2026. On January 26, 2026, we announced that our Board had declared a quarterly dividend of $0.07 per share for the first quarter of fiscal year 2026 that will be payable in May 2026. In the future, our Board may determine to reduce or eliminate our common stock dividend in order to fund investments for growth, repurchase shares or conserve capital resources.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMarsh McLennan Hikes Dividend 10% - Hampton Global Business Review (https://hgbr.org/marsh-mclennan-hikes-dividend-10/)\nciteturn11search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; \n\n  * July 9, 2025 |\n  * News\n\n# Marsh McLennan Hikes Dividend 10%\n\nMarsh McLennan boosts its quarterly dividend by 10%, signaling robust financial health and confidence in its diverse risk, strategy, and people advisory businesses. The move underscores the company’s strong belief in sustainable cash flow generation and commitment to shareholder returns.\n\nby Jack Smith |\n\nSHARE\n\nNEW YORK—In a move that speaks volumes about both its own robust financial health and the enduring resilience of the advisory sector, Marsh McLennan, the global titan in risk, strategy, and people, has announced a significant boost to its quarterly cash dividend.\n\nThe decision by its Board of Directors to increase the payout by a notable 10% — from $0.815 to $0.900 per share — is more than just a routine financial adjustment; it’s a confident declaration in a global economy still navigating choppy waters.\n\nPayable on August 15, 2025, to stockholders of record on July 24, 2025, this dividend hike signals a firm belief from the top that Marsh McLennan’s diverse portfolio of businesses continues to generate substantial, sustainable cash flow.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGLOBE LIFE INC. DECLARES DIVIDEND (https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/globe-life-inc-declares-dividend-302437556.html)\nciteturn11view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/globe-life-inc-declares-dividend-302437556.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 586\nL0: 【0†Accessibility Statement†www.cision.com】 【1†Skip Navigation】\nL1: \nL2: Search [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Search\nL5: \nL6: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] When typing in this field, a list of search results will appear and be automatically updated as you type.\nL7: \nL8: [Input: Search News Releases, Organizations, Resources, and Products]\nL9: \nL10: Searching for your content...\nL11: \nL12: No results 